WEBVTT

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.490
I'll survive!

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.150
You have an affinity for clubs.
You won in poker with them.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.840
Stay.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.670
I'll hit.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.530
Player busts.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.970
What should I have done?

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.180
The first order of business
is to learn that.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.420
I'm doing nothing but losing.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.110
It's according to plan.
Don't worry.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.860
You'll win.
I'll back you up.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.830
I'll display the basic strategy.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.830
Ten-value cards are the most
common type in this game.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:10.500
When the Dealer's upcard is a 5,
his probability of busting is 43%.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.980
Sit tight, and wait for your opponent
to self-destruct.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.360
Stay.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.890
Double down.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.850
That man is amazing.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:31.520
He isn't winning.
He's being allowed to win.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.380
It's dealer manipulation.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.380
Manipulation?

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.210
Right. Watch closely.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.970
All the players are going to
start leaving one at a time.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.010
Starting with that man.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.160
He's winning hands, but look at
how much money he's losing.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.920
That's what manipulation is.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.980
Throw off all
the players' decisions...

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.610
...and make them take actions
they'd never take otherwise.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.030
I didn't play very well, did I?

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.030
To go with the flow,
one has to pay the price.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.060
His losing was inevitable.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.230
He was manipulated into losing his entire
bankroll for the sake of momentary victories.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.070
I didn't see it at all.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.110
If you're aware of what's going on,
you can avoid the manipulation.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.630
Mine and the Doctor's, as well.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:27.010
I want to believe in you two.
Is that a bad thing?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.770
When all is said and done,
I'm a tool.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.800
I can only prove my usefulness
by having you use me.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.660
You're giving me more things I can do
by myself even when you aren't around.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.640
I want to use you.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.670
I'll never betray you again.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.050
I found myself a fine partner.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.680
Even money.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:11.640
When you have 21, it's a tie and there's
no payout if the dealer also gets 21.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.810
It's the sixth of this game's basic strategic
options, and is meant to prevent that.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.730
But the payout is a measly 1 to 1.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.320
It's the option to throw away
your hard-earned victory.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.340
It's not something that you
should choose right now.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.470
I'll begin a running count.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.760
Blackjack!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.220
That's amazing!

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.110
Have a wonderful evening, everyone.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.860
This dealer is making some kind
of pattern with the cards.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.370
You think he's manipulating
the card order?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.020
I can sense it.
He's doing something.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.410
All right. I'll read the cards with
calculations and the scent of our opponents.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.250
You read them with your senses.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:24.380
This is the true count. I'll log every card
and spot the right time to go all in.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.800
Until then, we'll manipulate
the dealer.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.240
Give him a taste of your mystique.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.890
Cross your legs.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:40.110
Look to the side so your cards
are to the left of your field of view.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.670
When people think of something
they like, they turn to the left.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.780
When they're nervous about something,
they look down and to the right.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.490
Once you know the patterns,
you can read someone's mind.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.620
He was reading me like that?

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.370
That's right.
And we'll use that against him.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.940
Look, they're like birds!

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.560
Gosh, it's so sharp
and pointy!

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.500
It seems really soft
for some reason.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.380
Still, hit me.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.400
So I'll stay.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.510
Hit me for sure.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.220
Wow, you're one of those people
with a gift for talking to the cards.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:18.140
I'm in the middle of an important deal!
What's the big idea, calling me away?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.420
You called him?

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.090
It's the rules, sir.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:25.090
Ashley? Chief?
Special Consultant?

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:29.910
Which of these high rollers making lots
of money has your panties in a twist?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.450
This flashy guy with the girl.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.660
According to the floor report,
they're uncle and niece.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.790
He's trying to insert ten-value cards into
the portion not used in the game.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.270
How many?

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.300
32.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:49.410
So, he's set aside the ten-value cards
from two decks.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:50.680
The nerve of this guy...

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.180
Hang on.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.470
He hasn't put them all in.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:56.970
Gotcha.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.730
Owner?

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:05.360
Deal with these two, Ashley!
Wipe out their luck your way!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.230
Acquaintances of yours, sir?

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:11.200
They're trying to completely
waste my time.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.580
I'm doing anything and everything
I can to escape time's curse.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.080
Don't you understand?!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:17.850
Yes, sir.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.850
I'm in the middle of some incredibly
important business.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.090
Don't let them get
any closer to me, got it?!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.750
Oeufcocque.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:30.340
Go in with the Doctor.
Do it.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.490
You'll never beat me
if you don't bet a lot.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.040
All right, challenge accepted!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:43.650
Split.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:47.270
Split.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.280
Split.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.070
Split.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.070
Split.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.830
We're within spitting distance now.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.360
Where the hell are you, Boiled?!

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.740
Searching for them.
What's wrong?

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:13.300
It's them!
 They're here right now!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.540
Just as I thought...

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:15.530
What?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.660
Answer me.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.480
Is whatever is involved in your
business deal there with you?{}

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:28.070
This is where my first Show was.
It all began here.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:35.260
I'll prove that you made the best choice.
That's my usefulness.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.330
I wanted to use you.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.000
That's all I wanted.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.840
Come back to me, Oeufcocque.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:53.760
Isn't it a little early
to be leaving, Bell Wing?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.760
Go for it. Bet it all.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.130
Stay.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:10.570
Stay.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.620
When the remaining cards are two sevens
and more than four eights,

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.000
...the odds of the player winning are 100%.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.620
That's the magic
of sevens and eights.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.940
Because the dealer stuck in
all the tens at the very end,

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:31.420
...I was able to predict
the remaining cards.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.630
The dealer brought this defeat
down on himself.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:36.550
It'll be too hard to carry
all these chips around.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:41.390
Let's just have them give us
 something bigger instead.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.140
A million-dollar chip, please.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.520
I'll see to it at once, sir.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:51.060
If you're there as the checker,
it'll convince the Association.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.780
If she has a system that can
net a million-dollar chip,

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.780
...you can bet
there will be copycats.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:59.950
So if the Association decides
to adopt my countermeasure,

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.950
...it'll mean
a big payday for us.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:06.710
If that happens, you and I won't have to
work for that nutjob anymore.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.820
I thought you liked this place.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.860
That was before I found out that
the owner was a rabid dog...

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.840
...who went around burning
fifteen year old girls to death.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:24.340
It's beyond me why the Association
still lets that man have a job.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:31.260
Fifteen... Oh, I see.
So that's why she's here.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:36.780
You standing in her way is a test
given to her by the Holy Spirit.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:40.660
You've given up being a spinner
and are a prophet now?

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:46.500
Have a little faith. I'm thankful
that I've been led to this place.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.920
By the way, how much do you
know about those two?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.570
Just the girl's name.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.920
Rune-Balot. What a sad name.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.550
Found it. The storage medium that
Shell's memories are recorded on.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.030
This is the first.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:22.490
Marlowe John Fever, you're fired.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.580
I signed a letter of
reference for you.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.040
Leave before the owner spots you.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:35.540
This troublemaker wanted to keep
playing, but we have rules here.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.120
I'm going to swap this for a fresh shoe.
Is that all right?

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.050
Of course.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.340
Just as I thought, you had
your sights set on a big target here.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.580
Bell Wing...

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:50.560
This is Ashley Harvest.
Our industry's idea of hired muscle.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:55.560
I'm here to observe how well
you can stand up to him.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.130
This man's luck
never runs counterclockwise.

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:03.200
He has no weak spots.
I suggest you remember that.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:03.950
I will.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.580
This table is now reserved
for you two.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:11.460
A little thank-you for getting
the cheat in the poker room,

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:15.960
...Bell Wing here,
and a talented dealer fired.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.590
Our own private table!
A bit extravagant, isn't it?

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.720
It's easier to win this way,
don't you think?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.010
I've never heard
of a dealer like you...

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.680
Here's hoping that looks
aren't deceiving.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.460
We have a draw.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:44.510
Stay.

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:45.530
Hit.

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:47.530
Stay.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.040
We have a draw.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:13:00.050
Sixteen draws in a row.
You don't see that every day...

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:04.490
A sign that your luck is an
even match for the casino's.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.050
You're formidable opponents, indeed.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:09.550
What is this man after?

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:10.990
I don't know.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:14.060
What's he thinking?
What's this scent I'm smelling?

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.330
What should I do?

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.650
For now, we'll hold him off
using the optimal strategies.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.940
It's not as if my card counting
is being blocked.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.830
We have a draw.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.850
He precisely ordered
over 300 cards while shuffling.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.860
His skill is hard to believe.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:42.590
Every single hand
ends in a draw...

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.360
You two have magnificent luck.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:48.970
Or perhaps there is some third party
who is giving you your luck?

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:55.850
Perhaps it's time
for a change in strategy.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.380
Hit.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:00.920
Hit.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:04.760
Hit me.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:08.490
Player busts.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:10.990
Hit.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:13.060
What should I do?

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:17.330
Stick with the optimal strategy.
Let the Doctor handle the frontal assault.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.000
Stay.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.010
We have a draw.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.880
It'll take more than one card
to get you to budge, huh?

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:30.740
Hit.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:31.780
Hit.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:33.290
Hit.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.310
Hit me.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.750
Player stays, I assume?

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:42.810
Stay.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.450
We have a draw.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:55.620
That's some countermeasure. Who else
besides you could possibly do that?

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.450
It's simply a matter of practice.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.710
For someone who shot down
every ball I threw,

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.270
...you're putting on
a boring show.

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:07.940
Chips don't mean anything
to you, right?

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:10.450
So why are you
holding back for?

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.930
Restraint is like a pile of shit.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:17.350
During a big match,
the stink distracts you.

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:23.610
Concentrate on the game. Don't forget
that she works for the casino, too.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:30.530
You're you. You don't need
to hold back for anyone.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.740
Hit me.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.370
Stay.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.870
Player loses, player draws.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.620
One can lose his luck
over the slightest thing.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:46.880
No one can laugh at someone
who's been abandoned by luck.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:52.260
I'll hand off my good luck to her,
and my bad luck to you.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.260
Feel free to rejoin the fight
whenever you like.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:56.260
Stay.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.020
Player loses.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:05.400
Stay.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.610
I made a mistake.
I'm sorry.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:15.620
Stop it.
He's manipulating you.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.780
He's trying to implant
a sense of defeat in you.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:22.870
But if I had done as you taught me
and not asked for that hit earlier,

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:25.190
...I would have had blackjack.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:27.230
You didn't make a mistake.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.630
It's my own fault for not being
able to read this man.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:34.010
My condolences, miss.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:40.270
By the way, you can't hear someone's voice
through that left glove of yours, can you?

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:41.750
How did you--

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:44.980
Bingo.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:51.030
You aren't speaking with the cards,
you're speaking with your left hand.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:57.720
I'm sorry, Oeufcocque...
I'm sorry.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:02.540
It's all right. Stay calm. He isn't
allowed to touch a guest's clothing.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:07.040
They don't have any means
of separating us.

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:13.610
Stay.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.060
Player loses.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.980
I have a question for you.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.230
What is it?

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.420
It's just a little icebreaker.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.700
It's no fun to play when the atmosphere
is this tense, don't you agree?

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.870
Let's say that you're driving down
a long road in your car.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.540
But the engine breaks down.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.460
Around you is nothing but desert.
What do you do?

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.880
I wait for help to arrive.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.260
So you would hitchhike.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.590
What would you do if you came across
someone who needed help?

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.510
If they look like they
can be trusted, I help them.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:05.450
I see.
Both are 50% answers.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.600
You're average.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.810
There are other answers?

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:14.780
Did you stop to consider that it could be
a carjacker pretending to be a hitchhiker?

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.320
You're saying that I should
never help anyone?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:20.070
By "50% answer," I mean that
your attitude changes...

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:23.080
...depending on which side
of the situation you're on.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:27.480
For example, if no one helps you,
you won't go looking for help.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:32.840
Or if you do help, you're prepared
to be killed by that person.

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:36.340
What would a 100% answer be?

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:40.180
If someone asks for help, you kill him.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.100
That person is prey.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.930
And if someone offers their help,
that person is also prey.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:51.770
This is a place where we can
legally steal from others.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.670
That is what gambling is.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:58.740
What is a sweet young lady like you
doing in such a place?

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:01.610
Were you born mute?

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:04.660
Or did you lose your voice
because of someone?

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.740
While hitchhiking, perhaps?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:15.130
Stay calm. I can't read his intentions.
Don't make any hasty moves.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.010
This man is testing me.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.850
To see whether or not
I'll play his game.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.560
Stop what you're doing.
Please trust me.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:31.190
I do. That's why I'm asking you
to please trust me.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:32.540
Balot!

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.700
Do I look like
I'm that easy to kill?

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:49.200
You're a formidable opponent.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:53.460
We probably wouldn't find anything
even if we searched your body.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:56.380
There might not have been
anything to begin with.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:20:00.010
In any case, you took off your gloves
of your own accord.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:03.410
Neither I nor the casino
forced you to do so.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:04.570
No.

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:13.350
When I say you're a formidable opponent,
I mean that you don't run or hide.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:17.300
Hit.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:19.480
Stay.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:23.740
Player loses.

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.430
Oeufcocque, do you read me?

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:31.640
I still seem to be able to transmit.
What are you up to?

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.750
I'm sorry. I just thought
that I had to do it.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.710
I have a favor to ask.
Do you mind?

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.510
If it's in my power.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:43.930
Add the numbers to my senses.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.390
Not the count?

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.010
That's too narrow.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:50.660
Something's bothering me,
something besides the numbers.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.020
I want to know what it is.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:56.460
Understood. I'll have the numbers
reflect your visualization as best I can.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.360
Manipulate them however you like.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.900
Thank you.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:02.130
Sure thing, Partner.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.140
Player busts.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:13.290
Player busts.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:36.390
Player busts.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.770
They're like birds flying...

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:41.270
Excuse me?

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:43.280
So hit me.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:47.860
Player busts.

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:55.390
It's pointy, so I want
to round it off.

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:56.250
Hit.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.230
It's incredibly pointy.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:00.690
Still, hit me.

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.360
It's getting pointier
and pointier.

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:03.000
Hit.

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:05.760
Hit.

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:08.760
Hit.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:12.370
Stay.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:17.270
A draw...

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:19.900
So it would seem.

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:24.730
Do you know why I am looking forward
to this next card?

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:28.030
If it's a king, you lose.
Especially if it's a spade.

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:30.280
All that card plucking
would be for nothing.

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:33.280
You saw through my shuffle?

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:38.730
No. But the cards have been in
your favor this whole time.

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:41.670
But now I have allies
of my own.

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:44.300
Not very many, it seems.

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:47.550
I don't need to win much.

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:54.890
I want to bet on clubs.
They're going to be on my side.

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:55.930
Understood.

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:57.540
Hit.

00:22:58.500 --> 00:22:59.620
Hit.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.380
Stay.

00:23:04.090 --> 00:23:05.190
You won!

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:06.940
Congratulations.

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:09.950
Next hand.

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:29.320
Hit.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.070
Hit.

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:34.660
Stay.

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:41.850
She did it!

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:45.610
Did you see that? Say what
you like about this girl,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:48.820
...but she knows what
it means to endure.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:54.120
Bell Wing... And here I thought
that you were on MY side.

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:57.490
It's no fun if the game
is over quickly.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:01.850
There's just one thing
that I want you to remember.

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:05.810
That thing I blurted out and tried to
teach you even if you already knew it.

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:08.190
About being ladylike?

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:13.030
Right. Be the person you ought to be.
Be who you're meant to be.

00:24:13.030 --> 00:24:15.390
Otherwise, you'll never be
able to talk to the cards.

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:20.370
If you can't talk to the cards, you'll never
be able to beat this man. Right?

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:21.890
Right.

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:26.400
That's better. You're far more
beautiful now than before.

00:24:26.670 --> 00:24:29.050
Thank you, Bell Wing.

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:34.410
I should have asked
someone else...

00:24:36.850 --> 00:24:39.410
It's hard to believe...

00:24:39.680 --> 00:24:42.500
You're beginning
to understand luck.

00:24:42.500 --> 00:24:47.670
I've spent my whole life trying to do so,
and you've done it in a mere hour.

00:24:49.710 --> 00:24:51.630
You're humble.

00:24:51.630 --> 00:24:55.410
Such people take coincidence
and turn it into the inevitable.

00:24:55.410 --> 00:24:58.430
Inevitability that will
allow them to survive.

00:24:58.430 --> 00:25:01.370
Have you ever
thought about luck?

00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:05.480
I used to think a lot
about how bad mine was.

00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:11.480
There's more to that hitchhiking story
I was telling earlier. May I continue?

00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:13.140
Of course.

00:25:13.140 --> 00:25:16.860
I had an older brother.
Two brothers against the world.

00:25:16.860 --> 00:25:19.370
He meant the world to me.

00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:24.500
But one day, he picked up a hitchhiker
in his car and was killed by him.

00:25:24.850 --> 00:25:29.670
He was forced into the trunk,
and was left out in the blazing sun.

00:25:29.670 --> 00:25:32.710
He was ravaged by dehydration
and respiratory distress,

00:25:32.710 --> 00:25:36.010
...and eventually died in the dark
when his strength gave out.

00:25:36.740 --> 00:25:42.060
After the funeral, my father and I went to
where my brother had been found.

00:25:42.060 --> 00:25:47.730
There, I climbed into the trunk my brother
had died in and had my father close it.

00:25:47.730 --> 00:25:49.520
I wanted to know what
my brother had felt.

00:25:50.440 --> 00:25:52.780
It was terrifying in there.

00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:57.530
As I frantically struggled there in the
pitch blackness, I heard my father's voice.

00:25:57.530 --> 00:26:00.530
"Pull the latch.
There's a latch inside."

00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:06.790
I found the latch.
And I survived in my brother's place.

00:26:07.270 --> 00:26:10.460
If only my brother
had known about that latch.

00:26:10.460 --> 00:26:15.170
If only he had had someone
to tell him it was there.

00:26:15.170 --> 00:26:18.970
If only he had been lucky enough
to save himself.

00:26:18.970 --> 00:26:23.180
If he'd had any one of those three,
my brother wouldn't have died.

00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:26.770
It's the people without those three
who lose first.

00:26:26.770 --> 00:26:29.770
I don't know which
of the three you have.

00:26:30.130 --> 00:26:35.150
But you've been spared because you do.
You mustn't forget that.

00:26:35.150 --> 00:26:36.510
I won't.

00:26:39.760 --> 00:26:41.030
Player wins.

00:26:41.410 --> 00:26:42.780
Player wins.

00:26:43.260 --> 00:26:44.910
Player wins.

00:26:47.770 --> 00:26:49.150
Balot...

00:26:49.600 --> 00:26:53.270
Sometimes it's more painful
to win than it is to lose.

00:26:53.270 --> 00:26:57.170
The more you win, the greater
the weight you have to carry.

00:26:59.990 --> 00:27:01.030
Hit.

00:27:02.620 --> 00:27:03.550
Stay.

00:27:03.950 --> 00:27:05.160
Draw.

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:06.560
Next hand.

00:27:07.160 --> 00:27:08.000
Hit.

00:27:09.350 --> 00:27:10.310
Hit.

00:27:11.790 --> 00:27:13.040
Stay.

00:27:14.320 --> 00:27:16.070
Player loses.

00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:21.390
No one will laugh at you
if you decide to quit now.

00:27:32.020 --> 00:27:33.460
Next hand.

00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:56.730
Double down.

00:28:04.450 --> 00:28:10.000
Congratulations. According to house rules,
triple sevens pay out 1.5 to 1.

00:28:16.860 --> 00:28:20.070
Tactics and strategy
are the key to victory.

00:28:20.070 --> 00:28:22.970
Tactics are the
individual decisions.

00:28:23.570 --> 00:28:24.910
What's the first?

00:28:24.910 --> 00:28:27.140
Stay. Don't take a card.

00:28:27.540 --> 00:28:28.540
Next?

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:31.230
Hit. Take another card.

00:28:31.230 --> 00:28:32.440
Third.

00:28:32.440 --> 00:28:36.690
Double down. Take one last extra card
and double your bet.

00:28:36.690 --> 00:28:37.920
And the fourth?

00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:40.440
Split. When you have
matching cards,

00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:43.110
...set out more chips and play them
as separate wagers.

00:28:43.110 --> 00:28:47.430
And surrender. Pay half your bet
and fold your hand.

00:28:47.430 --> 00:28:50.950
Strategy is the accumulation
of these five tactics.

00:28:50.950 --> 00:28:54.460
With timing and teamwork,
victory is assured.

00:28:57.610 --> 00:28:58.630
Even money.

00:29:02.340 --> 00:29:05.630
Even money?
But you're sure to win.

00:29:05.630 --> 00:29:11.020
In spite of that, you're going to throw away
a double payout and maximum victory?

00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:17.940
We're talking four million dollars. You're
really going to walk away from that payout?

00:29:19.090 --> 00:29:20.130
Yes.

00:29:22.590 --> 00:29:24.780
I didn't think you had it in you.

00:29:25.470 --> 00:29:29.740
Just now, I saw courage.
And humility.

00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:33.540
For the first time, I saw someone achieve
total victory with my own two eyes.

00:29:35.480 --> 00:29:40.130
I once died the same way
your brother did.

00:29:40.940 --> 00:29:46.800
But I had people who rescued me
from the locked car.

00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:52.260
To think that my cards
were defeated...

00:29:52.260 --> 00:29:54.000
I can't see the cards.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:57.060
The cards don't matter anymore.
This is your victory.

00:29:58.170 --> 00:29:59.810
Your perfect victory.

00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:18.960
If you don't mind, would you tell me
what you hope to find in those chips?

00:30:20.690 --> 00:30:27.010
I think I made a deal with someone.
I wanted to be able to do this on my own.

00:30:28.160 --> 00:30:30.340
You're like a mermaid.

00:30:30.340 --> 00:30:33.580
I just remembered a story about
a mermaid who gave her up voice...

00:30:33.580 --> 00:30:36.710
...to receive magic legs
that let her walk on land.

00:30:36.710 --> 00:30:39.920
I bet that she was
just as brave as you.

00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:42.920
The owner?

00:30:42.920 --> 00:30:47.220
Precisely. Too bad, I'd hoped to continue
the cool act a while longer.

00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:48.740
I'm really sorry, Bell Wing.

00:30:49.220 --> 00:30:54.240
Oh, please. You've been head over heels
for this girl for a dozen hands now.

00:30:55.950 --> 00:31:00.500
Please call the owner.
I want to return these chips to him.

00:31:04.070 --> 00:31:09.550
You had me fooled. You weren't trying
to break the bank at all, were you?

00:31:11.570 --> 00:31:15.510
The owner's days are numbered if you
have it out for him, young lady.

00:31:17.580 --> 00:31:22.020
I just hope that the spell on you
lasts for a long time.

00:31:29.430 --> 00:31:30.800
He's here.

00:31:32.260 --> 00:31:34.550
Cleanwill John October.

00:31:34.550 --> 00:31:38.040
Shell's business partner,
as well as the father of his fiancee.

00:31:46.960 --> 00:31:49.320
Take those back.

00:31:53.430 --> 00:31:56.390
You little whore that was born
in a garbage dump...

00:32:02.020 --> 00:32:06.800
Take only the yolk. Don't touch
the shell or the white.

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:08.460
But if you do--

00:32:08.460 --> 00:32:09.780
Return them at once.

00:32:17.810 --> 00:32:19.910
A wise choice!

00:32:27.770 --> 00:32:30.050
I gave you everything!

00:32:40.430 --> 00:32:43.810
I'll keep spinning
the wheel somewhere.

00:32:44.830 --> 00:32:47.310
If you're ever in the mood,
stop by and see me.

00:32:51.300 --> 00:32:52.320
I will.

00:33:13.300 --> 00:33:15.530
You sure you didn't
forget anything?

00:33:23.180 --> 00:33:24.560
I smell murderous intent!

00:33:26.150 --> 00:33:27.350
Crap! Boiled?!

00:33:27.940 --> 00:33:29.440
Balot, use me!

00:33:29.440 --> 00:33:32.990
Forget! This is as her primary physician!
Balot's already at her limit!

00:34:03.750 --> 00:34:05.480
Oeufcocque!

00:34:07.310 --> 00:34:08.460
Balot!

00:34:10.460 --> 00:34:11.600
Balot...

00:34:21.530 --> 00:34:23.600
Rune-Balot...

00:34:38.110 --> 00:34:41.550
Thank goodness...
She's stabilized.

00:34:41.550 --> 00:34:43.560
Abnormal skin fiber growth?

00:34:43.560 --> 00:34:45.060
The data says something's wrong.

00:34:45.790 --> 00:34:49.560
But given the situation she's in,
it's perfectly normal.

00:34:50.690 --> 00:34:53.150
We've got some hard work
ahead of us.

00:34:53.150 --> 00:34:55.570
After all, we have to pore over the
memories of a homicidal maniac.

00:34:56.990 --> 00:35:00.070
Let's just pray
that it's for the best.

00:35:13.710 --> 00:35:17.210
We'll use Shell's memories to establish
the process that led to his crimes.

00:35:18.150 --> 00:35:22.140
You and Oeufcocque should
be able to do it in a day.

00:35:22.140 --> 00:35:24.100
But are you really sure
you want to do this?

00:35:24.100 --> 00:35:27.310
I want to know.
I want to know why me.

00:35:27.310 --> 00:35:30.670
If I can find some answers,
any at all, it'll be enough.

00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:33.520
Balot is perfectly rational
about this, Doctor.

00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:34.840
Right.

00:35:35.670 --> 00:35:38.070
Okay, let's scramble some eggs.

00:36:19.210 --> 00:36:22.740
I'm begging you, I don't want
to go back to my father.

00:36:23.550 --> 00:36:25.990
I'll make you beautiful.

00:36:29.330 --> 00:36:32.500
We need to establish context.
There's no meaning.

00:36:32.500 --> 00:36:34.000
Let's go back to the entrance.

00:36:34.500 --> 00:36:37.840
Trouble will be knocking
on your door soon.

00:36:37.840 --> 00:36:40.380
This deal is for me alone.

00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:43.840
You had misgivings about
what you were given...

00:36:47.490 --> 00:36:51.020
A blue diamond.
That's my solution.

00:37:06.390 --> 00:37:10.580
Keep it up. Shell's motive for committing
murder is becoming clearer.

00:37:13.330 --> 00:37:16.830
There's nowhere that I
want to go back to...

00:37:17.940 --> 00:37:19.610
Why...?

00:37:19.610 --> 00:37:20.880
Why me?

00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:24.260
Why am I so afraid of her?!

00:37:24.630 --> 00:37:27.550
Hold yourself together.
That isn't your fear.

00:37:30.910 --> 00:37:36.350
I can't possibly know why that is.
I've already forgotten everything.

00:37:59.440 --> 00:38:02.170
There's nowhere that I
want to go back to...

00:38:02.820 --> 00:38:07.180
I promise. Even if I lose my
memories, I'll remember you.

00:38:07.880 --> 00:38:10.430
There's something that
I want you to hear.

00:38:10.430 --> 00:38:12.510
I'll remember you, no matter--

00:38:12.510 --> 00:38:14.700
I was raped by my father.

00:38:16.020 --> 00:38:19.400
Stop! Don't get drawn into it!
Calm down, Balot!

00:38:19.900 --> 00:38:21.210
Stop it, Doctor!

00:38:21.570 --> 00:38:24.820
Damn... Balot is stronger
than I expected.

00:38:25.440 --> 00:38:27.030
I'll make you beautiful!

00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:29.030
I'll make you
into something beautiful!

00:38:29.680 --> 00:38:33.240
This is wrong...
He didn't kill the first girl.

00:38:34.020 --> 00:38:37.040
We'll have to send her
all the way back to the very end.

00:38:38.250 --> 00:38:40.040
The first person he killed was...

00:38:46.530 --> 00:38:51.740
I had a processing specialist turn my
dead mother's ashes into a diamond.

00:38:52.370 --> 00:38:54.060
We've reached
the emotional trauma.

00:38:54.470 --> 00:38:56.220
Why... Why me?

00:38:56.640 --> 00:38:59.060
Mother, stop! Mother!

00:39:07.380 --> 00:39:09.260
23 hours.

00:39:09.720 --> 00:39:13.580
That's how much time has passed
since you laid down in there.

00:39:21.560 --> 00:39:23.090
Get some rest.

00:39:23.690 --> 00:39:28.300
You won't have any bad dreams.
Oeufcocque is right there with you.

00:39:41.080 --> 00:39:41.980
Good morning.

00:39:44.440 --> 00:39:46.480
The trial date's been set.

00:39:54.830 --> 00:39:56.970
I was a fool.

00:39:56.970 --> 00:40:00.160
If only I'd told you more of
what you needed to know...

00:40:00.940 --> 00:40:05.980
Please. Help me become a new person
one more time.

00:40:10.840 --> 00:40:13.010
I'll erase everything.

00:40:13.780 --> 00:40:16.260
Sexual molestation by the mother.

00:40:16.950 --> 00:40:21.230
When he was 18,
Shell killed his mother.

00:40:21.230 --> 00:40:25.150
He rigged her car and burned her to death
inside, making it look like an accident.

00:40:25.590 --> 00:40:29.230
Without that memory, it left him unable
to keep his emotions in check,

00:40:29.230 --> 00:40:32.070
...and that became the root
of his homicidal urges.

00:40:32.070 --> 00:40:36.530
Shell started to think what he
was doing made perfect sense.

00:40:36.530 --> 00:40:41.660
And so Shell selected girls with a past
identical to his own, and sacrificed them.

00:40:41.660 --> 00:40:46.630
I think it was after Shell's lover died.
A girl that Shell truly loved.

00:40:47.610 --> 00:40:51.630
It seemed to come as a real shock when
he learned that they had identical pasts.

00:40:52.090 --> 00:40:55.800
That the two of them
had chosen someone so similar.

00:40:56.320 --> 00:40:58.560
Shell didn't kill that girl.

00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:01.770
Despair resulting from sympathy, huh?

00:41:02.330 --> 00:41:07.060
In any event, this will cast doubt on
the usefulness of October Corp.

00:41:07.060 --> 00:41:11.400
Anyway, the loss of his memory turned
Shell into a bloodthirsty killer.

00:41:12.170 --> 00:41:16.360
Do you think Shell will stop killing
if he gets his memories back?

00:41:16.680 --> 00:41:21.040
It's possible. But he would
probably refuse.

00:41:21.040 --> 00:41:25.670
He didn't fight like you did.
He simply sought out victims.

00:41:25.670 --> 00:41:28.060
You two saved me.

00:41:29.150 --> 00:41:30.380
Thank you.

00:41:52.210 --> 00:41:54.950
Well, I suppose
that closes your case.

00:42:02.060 --> 00:42:05.790
It's from the public prosecutor.
A request for negotiations.

00:42:05.790 --> 00:42:08.580
The name on it is October Corp's
representative director.

00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:10.380
What does that mean?

00:42:10.380 --> 00:42:12.840
He's the man who was next
to Shell at the casino.

00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:16.720
He's requested negotiations
and information disclosure.

00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:22.600
They're scared that we might exploit your
case to expose their criminal activity.

00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:23.620
Exploit?

00:42:23.620 --> 00:42:28.520
Well, it means that the chips you won
give us that kind of leverage.

00:42:30.480 --> 00:42:31.630
What's this?

00:42:32.590 --> 00:42:35.590
It says that the lead negotiator
for the case is Boiled.

00:42:36.590 --> 00:42:40.160
Impossible. Boiled would
be working two contracts.

00:42:40.160 --> 00:42:41.160
Where's Shell?

00:42:42.100 --> 00:42:43.330
Out on bail.

00:42:43.330 --> 00:42:47.960
The prosecutor has him under surveillance,
but I have a bad feeling about this.

00:42:47.960 --> 00:42:48.520
Balot.

00:42:48.520 --> 00:42:49.120
Forget it.

00:42:49.770 --> 00:42:53.420
Do you want us to take the lead
and burn her even more?

00:42:53.420 --> 00:42:54.630
What are you talking about?

00:42:55.010 --> 00:42:59.380
Shell and his memories
are the only material we have.

00:42:59.380 --> 00:43:04.140
October Corp might want to eliminate Shell.
We have to protect him.

00:43:04.560 --> 00:43:09.390
I'm not sure I follow you. Does that mean
that I need to protect Shell?

00:43:09.890 --> 00:43:10.480
It does.

00:43:10.480 --> 00:43:11.520
Forget it.

00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:14.110
She's closed her own case.

00:43:14.110 --> 00:43:17.820
Her case belongs to her.
She chose this.

00:43:17.820 --> 00:43:21.470
Her Life Support Program
has been extended indefinitely.

00:43:21.470 --> 00:43:23.540
She's your user, so--

00:43:23.540 --> 00:43:25.520
Don't try to manipulate her!

00:43:26.310 --> 00:43:28.910
Thank you, Oeufcocque.

00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:33.290
I want to learn to be able
to use you properly.

00:43:33.980 --> 00:43:39.110
What lies ahead won't necessarily
be good for you.

00:43:39.110 --> 00:43:41.470
Maybe, but this is what I chose.

00:43:41.470 --> 00:43:46.600
To make it go even a little bit better,
teach me how you close cases.

00:43:46.600 --> 00:43:49.710
Show me how I can do it, too.

00:43:51.500 --> 00:43:52.900
Understood.

00:43:53.270 --> 00:43:56.900
Let's go.
Let's go close our case.

00:44:11.020 --> 00:44:12.900
I don't like the smell of this.

00:44:38.500 --> 00:44:41.550
Damn! It's Shell's fiancee.

00:44:41.550 --> 00:44:43.990
I still smell Shell's
murderous intent on her.

00:44:43.990 --> 00:44:47.080
This must be part of some rite
to become a new person.

00:44:49.890 --> 00:44:51.120
I smell murderous intent!

00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:17.860
W-We're just hired guns!
Come on, cut me some slack!

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:20.320
Call your employer.

00:45:20.920 --> 00:45:23.220
Wow, nicely done.

00:45:23.220 --> 00:45:24.320
Well...

00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:27.430
Yes. Yes, sir.

00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:34.330
That was a fascinating game
you played at the casino.

00:45:34.600 --> 00:45:38.210
The game is over.
You're under arrest, Mr. Cleanwill.

00:45:38.210 --> 00:45:42.240
Hardly. You have no proof that
I gave them their orders.

00:45:42.240 --> 00:45:44.590
More importantly, you should
agree to the negotiations.

00:45:45.010 --> 00:45:48.340
We're suing Shell, same as you.

00:45:48.340 --> 00:45:49.350
Come again?

00:45:49.780 --> 00:45:54.290
Shell-Septinos did undeserved
damage to our casino,

00:45:54.290 --> 00:45:58.400
...damaged our corporate image, and even
demanded that I share my assets.

00:45:58.400 --> 00:46:00.060
What a convenient excuse.

00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:02.540
Sharing family assets is only natural
where marriages are concerned.

00:46:02.540 --> 00:46:05.300
Marriage? Oh, right.

00:46:05.300 --> 00:46:09.370
I'm amazed that some other man
would want that girl...

00:46:17.770 --> 00:46:20.250
I'll make you beautiful...

00:46:20.250 --> 00:46:23.800
We even have
an excellent case worker.

00:46:23.800 --> 00:46:27.660
You children of 09 should fight
this out amongst yourselves.

00:46:27.660 --> 00:46:30.530
That bastard! Is he going to
let Shell be killed by Boiled?

00:46:31.490 --> 00:46:32.010
Balot!

00:46:33.660 --> 00:46:37.980
What are you doing? You'll be arrested
for hacking into a public system!

00:46:41.860 --> 00:46:45.190
Stop it! Follow proper procedure!
Don't lose control!

00:47:01.440 --> 00:47:03.340
No, Balot!

00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:07.010
Please! Let me kill this man!
And Shell!

00:47:07.490 --> 00:47:10.940
Let me kill them all!
I can die afterwards for all I care!

00:47:10.940 --> 00:47:13.740
Balot? Are you angry?

00:47:14.040 --> 00:47:15.910
Or are you sad?

00:47:15.910 --> 00:47:19.080
That girl was also like me.

00:47:19.710 --> 00:47:22.250
Like all the other girls Shell killed.

00:47:22.250 --> 00:47:25.690
The same?
You mean her father--

00:47:31.070 --> 00:47:34.490
Please... I don't care if I die!

00:47:34.490 --> 00:47:37.080
Please! Let me kill them!

00:47:38.730 --> 00:47:41.100
I can smell your soul.

00:47:41.400 --> 00:47:46.230
It makes me certain that if there's one
thing that I can believe in, it's you.

00:47:48.900 --> 00:47:52.110
I give myself over to you.

00:48:03.020 --> 00:48:04.770
To think you were in the same hotel...

00:48:04.770 --> 00:48:07.110
This sort of hobby is frowned upon.

00:48:07.110 --> 00:48:08.860
This is pretty blatantly illegal.

00:48:08.860 --> 00:48:10.740
This is private property!

00:48:11.280 --> 00:48:14.910
Then let's leave it to the police
to sort everything out.

00:48:15.890 --> 00:48:19.000
Let's go. There's still something
that we need to do.

00:48:25.380 --> 00:48:28.760
Cleanwill knew that his daughter would
be killed, and left her to her fate.

00:48:29.280 --> 00:48:32.550
This would cost Shell
his right to a case worker,

00:48:32.550 --> 00:48:36.260
...and he could contract Boiled
with no conflict of interest.

00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:39.060
This guy is way more burnt
than we are.

00:48:39.060 --> 00:48:42.440
I don't care what his reasons were!
That was his own daughter!

00:48:42.440 --> 00:48:47.480
If their "suit against Shell" scenario is still
in play, he hasn't been eliminated yet.

00:48:47.480 --> 00:48:49.650
We still have time to take him
into protective custody.

00:48:49.650 --> 00:48:52.650
Will he trust us, though?

00:48:52.650 --> 00:48:57.280
If Shell gets his memory back,
I'm sure that he won't kill anyone else.

00:49:02.580 --> 00:49:04.020
Boiled?!

00:49:04.650 --> 00:49:07.480
I've gotten an offer
from October Corp.

00:49:07.480 --> 00:49:10.940
Who gives a damn
about October Corp?

00:49:10.940 --> 00:49:14.490
I can become
a new person again now.

00:49:14.490 --> 00:49:20.160
I'm grateful to you. A little longer, and
I would've been killed by that woman.

00:49:20.160 --> 00:49:24.560
You're a true friend. Let's stay
in touch after this, Boiled.

00:49:24.560 --> 00:49:28.480
As part of the discovery process,
case workers are in your area.

00:49:28.480 --> 00:49:32.530
If they find you,
the tables will be turned.

00:49:32.530 --> 00:49:34.570
What are you talking about?

00:49:34.570 --> 00:49:38.600
I'm saying that you're my savior,
someone who would never betray me.

00:49:38.600 --> 00:49:39.950
I don't want to die.

00:49:42.680 --> 00:49:44.980
But you killed me anyway.

00:49:45.650 --> 00:49:47.710
What the hell was that, Boiled?!

00:49:47.710 --> 00:49:52.530
So, you're here. You're listening in over
this line, aren't you, Oeufcocque?

00:49:52.530 --> 00:49:55.220
What? I asked you
a question, Boiled!

00:49:55.530 --> 00:50:00.220
What's the sense in us fighting?
Back off from this, Boiled.

00:50:00.870 --> 00:50:05.000
You and I were created to bring as much
nothingness into the world as possible.

00:50:05.000 --> 00:50:10.060
I suspect that your current user is itching
for a chance at justifiable homicide, too.

00:50:10.710 --> 00:50:14.740
What good will come of killing Shell?
What will come of killing everyone?

00:50:15.050 --> 00:50:18.090
Creating things isn't my job.

00:50:18.550 --> 00:50:20.950
Boiled! Are you trying to kill me?!

00:50:21.720 --> 00:50:27.750
Mr. Shell. I think that we could have
been more than client and patron.

00:50:28.400 --> 00:50:31.380
It's unfortunate, but the
situation has changed.

00:50:31.380 --> 00:50:32.360
Boiled...

00:50:32.360 --> 00:50:35.630
I'm Oeufcocque-Penteano,
the case worker assigned to you.

00:50:37.070 --> 00:50:38.570
I'm taking you into protective--

00:50:46.080 --> 00:50:47.890
I didn't want to die.

00:51:14.110 --> 00:51:19.880
Give her your weapon, and the Life
Support Program will apply to you.

00:51:19.880 --> 00:51:21.090
Where are you?!

00:51:21.340 --> 00:51:23.260
Somewhere close.

00:51:25.290 --> 00:51:27.850
Do you know what
I'm doing, then?

00:51:29.020 --> 00:51:32.360
What's the point of that now?
This is your final chance.

00:51:32.630 --> 00:51:33.960
Shut up!

00:51:33.960 --> 00:51:37.940
I'm gonna show those idiots who sent
this woman after me how business is done!

00:51:38.470 --> 00:51:42.180
Oeufcocque.
My life is being threatened.

00:52:03.660 --> 00:52:06.600
I'm returning what you lost.

00:52:28.180 --> 00:52:30.850
No matter how rotten the egg,

00:52:30.850 --> 00:52:34.750
...if you warm it up,
it might come back to life.

00:52:37.690 --> 00:52:40.380
Crap, low-altitude flight paths
have been shut down!

00:52:40.380 --> 00:52:42.200
Boiled's behind this!

00:52:42.200 --> 00:52:45.510
He hired a ton of aerial survey choppers
and packed the airspace with them!

00:52:45.510 --> 00:52:49.140
I'm using special investigation authority
to move them, but it's taking time.

00:52:49.140 --> 00:52:50.640
We fell into his trap.
How do we handle this?

00:52:51.710 --> 00:52:53.640
Defense and retreat
are our only options.

00:52:54.040 --> 00:52:59.320
Even if a police squad comes, if they're in
October Corp's pocket, he'll be eliminated.

00:52:59.320 --> 00:53:00.900
I'll try to protect him.

00:53:01.550 --> 00:53:04.160
How long will it take
for you to get here?

00:53:04.160 --> 00:53:08.390
Two hours... No, one hour.
Have some faith in me.

00:53:09.890 --> 00:53:12.370
I do.
I won't run away.

00:53:12.370 --> 00:53:14.540
I WANT you to run away.
I'm begging you.

00:53:14.540 --> 00:53:17.060
I will. Once I'm done.

00:53:17.060 --> 00:53:19.400
I'll be there soon
to pick you up, okay?

00:53:21.240 --> 00:53:23.220
What do you have in mind?

00:53:29.330 --> 00:53:31.290
Bye-bye, Shell.

00:53:41.210 --> 00:53:44.260
You're going for
a direct confrontation?

00:53:46.260 --> 00:53:49.240
There were lots of people
I wanted to be loved by.

00:53:49.240 --> 00:53:52.700
But you're the only one
I ever wanted to love.

00:53:54.020 --> 00:53:58.700
We won't kill. We won't BE killed.
We won't let him kill, either.

00:53:58.700 --> 00:54:03.090
Because the man who's coming
used to be your friend.

00:54:03.090 --> 00:54:04.760
I'll try to find a way.

00:54:05.110 --> 00:54:10.830
We won't kill. We won't be killed.
We won't let him kill.

00:54:10.830 --> 00:54:12.220
That's going to be difficult.

00:54:13.620 --> 00:54:16.230
But it's worth making the attempt.

00:54:20.250 --> 00:54:23.230
I've found myself a fine partner.

00:54:29.930 --> 00:54:31.990
You've heard about my methods?

00:55:20.150 --> 00:55:21.520
That's enough, Boiled!

00:55:45.380 --> 00:55:49.110
Twee and the others were happy to
find someone like himself in you.

00:55:49.110 --> 00:55:50.240
So am I.

00:55:53.660 --> 00:55:57.620
I'm going to seal away
those powers of yours.

00:56:14.740 --> 00:56:17.430
It's a weapon that uses EM waves
to trigger pain in the skin!

00:56:17.430 --> 00:56:20.290
Turn off the pain!
Snark your own body!

00:56:27.420 --> 00:56:29.300
I don't want to die...

00:57:21.980 --> 00:57:24.580
It'll take more than that
to stop me.

00:57:25.440 --> 00:57:27.590
He's using his pseudogravity
as a makeshift leg...

00:58:00.760 --> 00:58:03.620
W...a...rm...

00:58:15.420 --> 00:58:18.410
Let's see you stop
the nothingness that is me.

00:58:31.770 --> 00:58:37.530
She did well. You should be the one
to finish it, Oeufcocque.

00:58:37.530 --> 00:58:39.430
Stop it, Boiled!

00:58:47.730 --> 00:58:48.960
Oeufcocque?!

01:00:08.390 --> 01:00:09.540
Oeufcocque...

01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:33.670
Your case is now concluded.

01:00:33.670 --> 01:00:39.170
I'd say that we deserve any anger you have
over being put in danger, but, well...

01:00:39.170 --> 01:00:43.490
The way this wrapped up
hit us pretty hard.

01:00:45.350 --> 01:00:48.450
Would you mind
staying with Oeufcocque?

01:00:49.180 --> 01:00:51.210
That's what he said, too.

01:00:51.210 --> 01:00:52.520
Boiled said that?

01:00:52.520 --> 01:00:54.830
Would it be okay if I went
for a drive for a bit?

01:00:54.830 --> 01:00:57.980
There's something else that
I need to tell Oeufcocque.

01:00:57.980 --> 01:01:00.240
Boiled said something else to you?

01:01:00.780 --> 01:01:03.570
"Now I can finally sleep."

01:01:04.530 --> 01:01:06.890
I was involved
in developing that, too.

01:01:06.890 --> 01:01:10.390
We made it so he'd never
have to sleep again.

01:01:13.210 --> 01:01:19.270
There's a lot of work to do. So we ought
to save the grieving for later.

01:02:11.770 --> 01:02:13.410
Would you mind holding me?

01:02:13.410 --> 01:02:15.210
Oeufcocque?

01:02:15.600 --> 01:02:19.710
I want to be held
a little more... By you.

01:02:22.440 --> 01:02:24.740
Let's cry together, Oeufcocque.

01:02:25.900 --> 01:02:31.120
To make the sadness
go away, just a little bit.
